#import "letterhead.typ": *
#show: form.with(id: "birth-certificate-waiver")

When no birth certificate is on file for an applicant who was born in a state or territory of the United States, a justice of the peace may, in extenuating circumstances, for good cause shown, and after a hearing, order an issuing official in the parish where the court sits to issue the marriage license without it. R.S. 9:227 and 9:228(B).

== Applicant

#field[Full name]

#field[Address]

#grid(columns: (1fr, 1fr), field[Telephone], field[Email])

#grid(columns: (1fr, 1fr), field[Date of birth], field[State or territory of birth])

#field[Name of the person you intend to marry]

Why there is no birth certificate on file:

#lines(2)

*Attach both of these.*

#item[A letter signed by the registration authority of the place of birth, under its raised seal or stamp, stating that a thorough search was made and that no birth record was located. R.S. 9:227.]

#item(field[Other proof of the facts of birth])

I ask the court to order that a marriage license be issued without a birth certificate. The order is directed to the issuing official in #office.parish Parish. Bring to the hearing everything else the clerk of court requires for the license.

#grid(
  columns: (3fr, 2fr),
  signature[Signature of applicant],
  signature[Date],
)

#order-page[Order]

#grid(columns: (3fr, 2fr), field[Applicant], field[Hearing held on (date)])

After a hearing, the court finds extenuating circumstances and good cause. The court finds that the parties have complied with all other requirements, including presentation of the letter required by R.S. 9:227 and other competent evidence that the applicant was born in a state or territory of the United States.

IT IS ORDERED that the official who issues marriage licenses in #venue, issue a marriage license to

#field[] #h(0.4em) and #h(0.4em) #field[]

without the applicant submitting a birth certificate. R.S. 9:228(B).

#field[Signed at #office.address.city, Louisiana, on (date)]

#justice-signature

This order must be attached to the marriage application.
